message.content:
On the lateral chest X-ray, there is a triangular opacity in the posterior inferior lung field with loss of the posterior hemidiaphragm silhouette and increased density overlying the lower thoracic spine. These findings are characteristic of left lower lobe atelectasis (retrocardiac collapse). There is no anterior opacity or superior displacement of fissures to suggest upper lobe involvement.

Uncertainty: Low; classic retrocardiac triangle sign present.

{"answer":"A. left lower lobe pulmonary atelectasis","reason":"Lateral view shows retrocardiac triangular opacity with posterior diaphragmatic silhouette loss, specific for LLL collapse."}

